    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186087866,
      "id": "7de671ee-7bba-54ce-bec2-d2d6f5569f4a",
      "title": "Writing First-Order Linear ODEs in Standard Form"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "def57922-3e23-5536-a4f2-8cd38540efd3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y + 6 x^{2} y=- 3 x y^{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nAssume $y\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y + 6 x^{2} y=- 3 x y^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y + 6 x^{2} y + 3 x y^{2}=0 \\\\ y (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 6 x^{2} + 3 x y)=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 6 x^{2} + 3 x y=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(3 x)}_{P(x)}y=\\underbrace{- 6 x^{2}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 3 x y=- 6 x^{2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=3 x$ and $Q(x)=- 6 x^{2}.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "401d673f-7959-5247-a1b3-7753ce2fa7c8",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "d0dc5f07-9dc1-5519-b242-3180c3a3f32f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 5 x y=- 2 x^{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e4364783-110d-5586-86e1-c1c8f6243f34",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 8 x y=- 7 x^{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "3e1bd63f-d022-5c91-a143-22afb965fc05",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 3 x y=- 6 x^{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "b6e1e07c-3bf2-5897-991d-ecc78d7f17c5",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + x y=- 3 x^{2}"
