    "question": {
      ":question/id": "faec6066-8d0b-5136-9e65-8af0794b8e68",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{10 x} + 7 x - 3 y e^{5 x}=0\\,.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{10 x} + 7 x - 3 y e^{5 x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{10 x} - 3 y e^{5 x}=- 7 x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- 3 e^{- 5 x})}_{P(x)}y=\\underbrace{- 7 x e^{- 10 x}}_{Q(x)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=- 3 e^{- 5 x}$ and $Q(x)=- 7 x e^{- 10 x}.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "9c5f9ace-d720-5e0f-8c52-2ca356c94253",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
